<title>ITALY: Europe car sales seen 0.5 pct down in May - Anfia.</title>
<headline>Europe car sales seen 0.5 pct down in May - Anfia.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Despite the strong 43.2 percent jump in Italian new car registrations in May, the overall European car market slipped 0.5 percent to 1,156,200 units, provisional data from Italian carmakers' association Anfia showed.</p>
<p>Anfia said in a statement that excluding Italy the fall was 7.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>France posted the biggest drop in May, Anfia said, with a 22.6 percent fall while the German market fell 8.8 percent.</p>
<p>But the British market grew 2.0 percent and Spain rose 6.9 percent.</p>
<p>Cumulative sales for the first five months of this year showed a 22.6 percent fall in France and a 4.2 percent decline in Germany. But the British market increased by 4.8 percent and Spain by 9.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
